invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: chacha20.c's use_avx2 reads CH_CPU_VAES in place of CH_CPU_AVX2, so a
  session whose caller found AVX2 and no VAES runs SSE2, and one whose
  value held CH_CPU_VAES alone would run the AVX2 kernel. A value with
  both bits or neither behaves the same, and the object holds both calls,
  so no vector and no build check notices.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into each kernel under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds it for x86-64 and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0;
